se_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127069" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c4576c2fb38c2b66c8cbe2a8cadc680e0a866b52d487a20a08bcf659fd85cb4" "basis" 1561 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the straight line with the vector equation\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Find the Cartesian equation of this line." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c4576c2fb38c2b66c8cbe2a8cadc680e0a866b52d487a20a08bcf659fd85cb4" "basis" 1561 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We have the vector equation \n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $P(-2,3,3)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨2,-5,3⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-2)}{2}=\\frac{y-3}{-5}=\\frac{z-3}{3}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+2}{2}=\\frac{y-3}{-5}=\\frac{z-3}{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c4576c2fb38c2b66c8cbe2a8cadc680e0a866b52d487a20a08bcf659fd85cb4" "basis" 1561 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080ba4d1769da3809cbf2ab4e44f58784d7dd89caeba612e18774fa2b95f178e" "basis" 1561 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c4576c2fb38c2b66c8cbe2a8cadc680e0a866b52d487a20a08bcf659fd85cb4" "basis" 1561 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x+2}{-2}=\\frac{y-3}{5}=\\frac{z+3}{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c4576c2fb38c2b66c8cbe2a8cadc680e0a866b52d487a20a08bcf659fd85cb4" "basis" 1561 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127397" "field" "selection" "attribute