ation" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "None of the listed"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/state.json" "file_sha256" "511b2fb557b8eb12ca669cf6b53992f7eb13b53e06b7c0fb3fd9d8a7807fc703" "basis" 2007 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{y-6}{10}=\\frac{z+2}{3},\\,x=-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/state.json" "file_sha256" "511b2fb557b8eb12ca669cf6b53992f7eb13b53e06b7c0fb3fd9d8a7807fc703" "basis" 2007 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the straight line with the parametric equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-2t \\\\ y=-5t \\\\ z=1-t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Find the Cartesian equation of this line." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/state.json" "file_sha256" "511b2fb557b8eb12ca669cf6b53992f7eb13b53e06b7c0fb3fd9d8a7807fc703" "basis" 2007 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3-2t \\\\ -5t \\\\ 1-t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2t \\\\ -5t \\\\ -t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThis implies that the given line passes through the point $P(3,0,1)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-2,-5,-1⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{-2}=\\frac{y-0}{-5}=\\frac{z-1}{-1}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{-2}=\\frac{y}{-5}=\\frac{z-1}{-1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/state.json" "file_sha256" "511b2fb557b8eb12ca669cf6b53992f7eb13b53e06b7c0fb3fd9d8a7807fc703" "basis" 2007 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2d544dca39e67026fca4e2f5913c8e174cb142d54c7a9af77d54db6a8e4ea1aa" "basis" 2007 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy