12ca669cf6b53992f7eb13b53e06b7c0fb3fd9d8a7807fc703" "basis" 2007 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that the line passes through the points $P(-1,4,5)$ and $Q(7,-1,2).$ Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. Let's consider the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ which is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨7,-1,2⟩-⟨-1,4,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,-5,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point $P$ and the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, we have that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the given line is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-1)}{8}=\\frac{y-4}{-5}=\\frac{z-5}{-3}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{8}=\\frac{y-4}{-5}=\\frac{z-5}{-3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/state.json" "file_sha256" "511b2fb557b8eb12ca669cf6b53992f7eb13b53e06b7c0fb3fd9d8a7807fc703" "basis" 2007 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2d544dca39e67026fca4e2f5913c8e174cb142d54c7a9af77d54db6a8e4ea1aa" "basis" 2007 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062714/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127466" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/questi