-7,-5⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-10}{3}=\\frac{y-0}{-7}=\\frac{z-(-6)}{-5}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-10}{3}=\\frac{y}{-7}=\\frac{z+6}{-5}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083592/state.json" "file_sha256" "79b531f4a33a8e6ecdac0b273aeb259d8b4cc6381e4caa988d49014db4c079a0"} {"question" "q-71028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083592/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f459ebae02c303ffbdaf1e7e6d5d50f6fa0548822275602509ac63b3920a721f"} {"question" "q-71028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083592/state.json" "file_sha256" "79b531f4a33a8e6ecdac0b273aeb259d8b4cc6381e4caa988d49014db4c079a0"} {"question" "q-71028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x+10}{3}=\\frac{y}{-7}=\\frac{z-6}{-5}"] ["math" "\\frac{x+3}{10}=\\frac{z-5}{-6},\\,y=7"] ["math" "\\frac{x-10}{3}=\\frac{y}{-7}=\\frac{z+6}{-5}"] ["math" "\\frac{x-3}{10}=\\frac{z+5}{-6},\\,y=-7"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{3}=\\frac{y}{-7}=\\frac{z}{-5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083592/state.json" "file_sha256" "79b531f4a33a8e6ecdac0b273aeb259d8b4cc6381e4caa988d49014db4c079a0"} {"question" "q-71028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x-10}{3}=\\frac{y}{-7}=\\frac{z+6}{-5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083592/state.json" "file_sha256" "79b531f4a33a8e6ecdac0b273aeb259d8b4cc6381e4caa988d49014db4c079a0"} {"question" "q-127410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the straight line with the parametric equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-2t \\\\ y=-5t \\\\ z=1-t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Find the Cartesian equation of this line." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083592/state.json" "file_sha256" "79b531f4a33a8e6ecdac0b273aeb259d8b4cc6381e4caa988d49014db4c079a0"} {"question" "q-127410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3-2t \\\\ -5t \\\\ 1-t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2t \\\\ -5t \\\\ -t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThis implies that the given line passes through the point $P(3,0,1)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-2,-5,-1⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{-2}=\\frac{y-0}{-5}=\\frac{z-1}{-1}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{-2}=\\frac{y}{-5}=\\frac{z-1}{-1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083592/state.json" "file_sha256" "79b531f4a33a8e6ecdac0b273aeb259d8b4cc6381e4caa988d49014db4c079a0"} {"question" "q-127410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Cour